# Normalize every text file to LF in the index and on checkout. Later lines win, so the narrower
# overrides below take precedence over this catch-all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pin the line ending per type rather than leaving it to auto-detection, and give git a C#-aware
# hunk header for .cs files.
*.cs text eol=lf diff=csharp
*.csproj text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.slnx text eol=lf

# linguist-generated drops these from the language statistics and collapses them in GitHub diffs.
# src/Whisparr3.Net/ is openapi-generator output, spec/openapi.raw.json is a captured spec, and
# spec/openapi.generated.json is generator/preprocess-spec.ps1 output. All three are generated
# bulk that no reviewer reads line by line.
# Deliberately not the binary macro: it expands to -diff -merge -text, which would render the spec
# delta as "Binary files differ" and destroy the reviewability the capture exists for. That reason
# applies to the patched spec's refresh diff exactly as it applies to the capture.
# Two files are deliberately absent from this list, for one reason. generator/operation-ids.json
# is committed source, and marking it generated would collapse in review the diff PREP-05 exists
# to expose. spec/transform-report.txt is generated, but D-13 makes it a review artifact for a
# human reading a spec-refresh PR and therefore something that must be read as a diff, which is
# the one thing linguist-generated takes away.
src/Whisparr3.Net/** linguist-generated
spec/openapi.raw.json linguist-generated
spec/openapi.generated.json linguist-generated
.openapi-generator/FILES linguist-generated

# Explicit so `* text=auto` cannot reclassify it.
*.png binary
